      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792736632920,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Tree is a Non-Linear Data Structure .\n\n2. Tree is used situation where we have to arrange\ndata in hierarchial manner .\n\n3. Every level of Tree has NODES , and every\nNODES can have CHILD NODE . TREE itself have a\nsingle top level NODE called as ROOT NODE .",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Tree is a Non-Linear Data Structure .\n\n2. Tree is used situation where we have to arrange data in hierarchial manner .\n\n3. Every level of Tree has NODES , and every NODES can have CHILD NODE . TREE itself have a single top level NODE called as ROOT NODE .",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
